==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Etymology 1===
According to Aikio (2020), possibly from {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*satu}}, derived from an unattested verb {{suffix|fi||alt1=*sate-|-u}}, related to {{cog|sma|soetedh||to tell something frightening}} and {{cog|sma|soete||frightening story}}. Alternatively, possibly an obscure derivation from {{m|fi|sattua}}; alternatively derived from {{m|fi|sataa}}, in which case the original meaning was "fall" and the semantic development would be comparable to that of {{ncog|de|Fall||case}} (< {{m|de|fallen||to fall}}).

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[fairy tale]]
# [[tale]] {{gloss|idle story}}
# [[fable]] {{gloss|fictitious narrative intended to enforce some useful truth or precept}}

